Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• `date`: restrict the analysis to July‑2017 tables (20170701‑20170731).  
• `fullVisitorId`: identify a unique visitor.  
• `hits`: repeated field that contains every hit during a session.  
• `hits.type`: select only ecommerce “ITEM” hits (the moment an item is recorded as purchased).  
• `hits.item.productName`: the product that was bought.  
• `hits.item.itemQuantity`: the quantity of the product in the hit.  

Typical conditions that will be used  
– `_TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170701' AND '20170731'`  (when the wildcard is used).  
– `hits.type = 'ITEM'` (keep only item‑purchase hits).  
– `LOWER(hits.item.productName) LIKE '%youtube%'` (find YouTube‑related items).  
– `LOWER(hits.item.productName) NOT LIKE '%youtube%'` exclude YouTube items.  

Below are 10 exploratory → progressively more complete BigQuery SQL statements (each limited to 20 rows) that help reach the final answer.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at one July‑2017 table to see ecommerce ITEM hits and their columns.
SELECT
  fullVisitorId,
  hits.item.productName,
  hits.item.itemQuantity
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_20170710`,
UNNEST(hits) AS hits
WHERE hits.type = 'ITEM'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: List distinct product names purchased on 5 July 2017.
SELECT DISTINCT hits.item.productName
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_20170705`,
UNNEST(hits) AS hits
WHERE hits.type = 'ITEM'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Show sample YouTube‐related products bought on 10 July 2017.
SELECT DISTINCT hits.item.productName
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_20170710`,
UNNEST(hits) AS hits
WHERE hits.type = 'ITEM'
  AND LOWER(hits.item.productName) LIKE '%youtube%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Retrieve visitors who bought any YouTube product on 29 July 2017.
SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_20170729`,
UNNEST(hits) AS hits
WHERE hits.type = 'ITEM'
  AND LOWER(hits.item.productName) LIKE '%youtube%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Show all items (including YouTube) purchased by those visitors on the same day.
WITH yt_buyers AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_20170729`,
  UNNEST(hits) AS hits
  WHERE hits.type = 'ITEM'
    AND LOWER(hits.item.productName) LIKE '%youtube%'
)
SELECT
  s.fullVisitorId,
  hits.item.productName,
  hits.item.itemQuantity
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_20170729` AS s,
UNNEST(s.hits) AS hits
WHERE hits.type = 'ITEM'
  AND s.fullVisitorId IN (SELECT fullVisitorId FROM yt_buyers)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Aggregate quantity of NON‑YouTube items bought by YouTube‑product visitors (single day).
WITH yt_buyers AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_20170729`,
  UNNEST(hits) AS hits
  WHERE hits.type = 'ITEM'
    AND LOWER(hits.item.productName) LIKE '%youtube%'
)
SELECT
  hits.item.productName,
  SUM(hits.item.itemQuantity) AS total_qty
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_20170729` AS s,
UNNEST(s.hits) AS hits
WHERE hits.type = 'ITEM'
  AND s.fullVisitorId IN (SELECT fullVisitorId FROM yt_buyers)
  AND LOWER(hits.item.productName) NOT LIKE '%youtube%'
GROUP BY hits.item.productName
ORDER BY total_qty DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Roll the same aggregation over ALL July 2017 tables with a wildcard.
WITH july AS (
  SELECT *
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_201707*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '01' AND '31'   -- keeps only July tables
), yt_buyers AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId
  FROM july, UNNEST(hits) AS hits
  WHERE hits.type = 'ITEM'
    AND LOWER(hits.item.productName) LIKE '%youtube%'
)
SELECT
  hits.item.productName,
  SUM(hits.item.itemQuantity) AS total_qty
FROM july AS s, UNNEST(s.hits) AS hits
WHERE hits.type = 'ITEM'
  AND s.fullVisitorId IN (SELECT fullVisitorId FROM yt_buyers)
  AND LOWER(hits.item.productName) NOT LIKE '%youtube%'
GROUP BY hits.item.productName
ORDER BY total_qty DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Same as #7 but returning also number of distinct buyers per product.
WITH july AS (
  SELECT *
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_201707*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '01' AND '31'
), yt_buyers AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId
  FROM july, UNNEST(hits) AS hits
  WHERE hits.type = 'ITEM'
    AND LOWER(hits.item.productName) LIKE '%youtube%'
)
SELECT
  hits.item.productName,
  COUNT(DISTINCT s.fullVisitorId) AS distinct_buyers,
  SUM(hits.item.itemQuantity)    AS total_qty
FROM july AS s, UNNEST(s.hits) AS hits
WHERE hits.type = 'ITEM'
  AND s.fullVisitorId IN (SELECT fullVisitorId FROM yt_buyers)
  AND LOWER(hits.item.productName) NOT LIKE '%youtube%'
GROUP BY hits.item.productName
ORDER BY total_qty DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Validate that the top product keeps the lead each day (daily totals).
WITH july AS (
  SELECT *
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_201707*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '01' AND '31'
), yt_buyers AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId
  FROM july, UNNEST(hits) AS hits
  WHERE hits.type = 'ITEM'
    AND LOWER(hits.item.productName) LIKE '%youtube%'
)
SELECT
  date,
  hits.item.productName,
  SUM(hits.item.itemQuantity) AS daily_qty
FROM july AS s, UNNEST(s.hits) AS hits
WHERE hits.type = 'ITEM'
  AND s.fullVisitorId IN (SELECT fullVisitorId FROM yt_buyers)
  AND LOWER(hits.item.productName) NOT LIKE '%youtube%'
GROUP BY date, hits.item.productName
ORDER BY date, daily_qty DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: FINAL answer – highest‑quantity non‑YouTube product bought by YouTube purchasers in July‑2017.
WITH july AS (
  SELECT *
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_201707*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '01' AND '31'
), yt_buyers AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId
  FROM july, UNNEST(hits) AS hits
  WHERE hits.type = 'ITEM'
    AND LOWER(hits.item.productName) LIKE '%youtube%'
)
SELECT
  hits.item.productName AS top_product,
  SUM(hits.item.itemQuantity) AS total_quantity
FROM july AS s, UNNEST(s.hits) AS hits
WHERE hits.type = 'ITEM'
  AND s.fullVisitorId IN (SELECT fullVisitorId FROM yt_buyers)
  AND LOWER(hits.item.productName) NOT LIKE '%youtube%'
GROUP BY top_product
ORDER BY total_quantity DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

Each query is capped with `LIMIT 20` (except query #10 which returns only the winner) and can be run sequentially to understand the data, refine the logic, and finally obtain the required product with the largest total quantity bought by visitors who purchased any YouTube‑related item in July 2017.
